.TH PORTS 1
.SH NAME
ports \\- enumerate local TCP and UDP listeners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ports
ports [--port NUMBER] [--transport tcp|udp] [--format json|ndjson]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports Linux listener evidence and best-effort owning process information.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBports --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
